l3: Serialise FipNamespace creation per external network

get_fip_ns looked up, built and stored the FipNamespace with no lock,
so pool workers for different routers on one external network could
each build their own during a fullsync and hand two routers the same
link-local pair. Hold one agent-wide lock across get, build and store.

Building under the lock serialises the first fullsync for an external
network by the cost of the FipNamespace constructor, once; later calls
only take the lock for a dictionary lookup, which is acceptable.

